 "intro": "Ilerda (Lleida) on the river Sicoris, Spain, 49 BC, at the start of the civil war. You are Julius Caesar, who has crossed the Rubicon and taken Italy. Pompey’s legates Afranius and Petreius hold Spain with five legions.",
 "debrief": "In Caesar’s account, a flood swept away his bridges and cut him off, until he built light boats like those he had seen in Britain and re-bridged the river. When the Pompeians retreated toward the Ebro, his infantry waded the river and outmarched them to the hills. Cut off from water, and with soldiers of both sides fraternising, the Pompeian army surrendered. Caesar let them go home or join him freely. He had won Spain almost without bloodshed. The other choices are what-ifs.",
